**Change Summary**:
- **Native ARM64 Support**: Added native Windows on ARM (aarch64) builds and installers; installers and portable archives are named per architecture (x64/arm64); the installer validates the target architecture (arm64 packages install only on arm64 systems); the About page shows the running architecture suffix (.x64/.arm64); arm64 automatically uses the matching distro mirror list;
- **Distro Notes**: Added a notes field in distro settings, displayed on the distro card;
- **Backup & Export Directory**: Added a "Default backup & export directory" setting, independent of the distro installation directory; export/compression backups prefer this directory;
- **Device ID & Request Metadata**: Added a randomly generated UUID device ID; all API requests now carry the software version, OS language, and device ID headers;
- **Cold-start & Sort Fix**: Fixed loss of distro drag-sort order caused by slow WSL VM cold starts;
- **Build & Release**: Build scripts accept an -Arch parameter to distinguish x64/arm64; release workflows split/renamed; winget now also submits the arm64 installer;
- **Other Fixes**: Updated proxy-save success message (reopen the terminal to apply); unified config file field naming style; dependency upgrades; fixed a path issue in distro settings;


---

Special thanks to @NekoMirra for testing and validating the ARM64 build — your feedback made native Windows on ARM support possible.


**Full Changelog**: https://github.com/owu/wsl-dashboard/compare/v0.11.0...v0.12.0

## 🧰 WebMCP

New [page.webmcp](https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-page#page-webmcp) and [frame.webmcp](https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-frame#frame-webmcp) give access to the tools that a page registers through the experimental [WebMCP](https://playwright.dev/docs/api/class-webmcp) browser API, so you can test them like any other part of your app:

```js
const browser = await chromium.launch({ args: ['--enable-features=WebMCP'] });
const page = await browser.newPage();
await page.goto('https://example.com');

for (const tool of await page.webmcp.tools())
  console.log(tool.name, tool.description);

const result = await page.webmcp.callTool('add', { a: 2, b: 40 });
console.log(result.content[0].text); // "42"
```

[Playwright MCP](https://playwright.dev/docs/getting-started-mcp) also supports WebMCP by default, with page-defined tools offered to the agent as `webmcp_<tool>`. Pass `--no-webmcp` to opt out.

[`playwright-cli`](https://playwright.dev/docs/getting-started-cli) exposes them as well:

```bash
playwright-cli webmcp-list
playwright-cli webmcp-call search_catalog --params '{"query":"cats"}'
```

## 🎬 Better videos

Videos can now be recorded at a custom frame rate, and the decorations for actions are styled with plain CSS:

```js
// playwright.config.ts
import { defineConfig } from '@playwright/test';

export default defineConfig({
  use: {
    video: {
      mode: 'on',
      size: { width: 1920, height: 1080 },
      fps: 60,
      show: {
        actions: {
          style: {
            point: 'width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: 50%; background: red',
            highlight: 'outline: 2px solid #333; background: rgba(0, 128, 255, .15)',
            title: 'font-size: 16px',
          },
        },
      },
    },
  },
});
```

